{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS"]]},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"abstract":[{"text":"Pick the sparse-set or the archetype storage for a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","type":"reference"},{"text":", and know what changes.","type":"text"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"text":" keeps its entities and components in one of two storages, chosen when it is created:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let nexus = Nexus()                       \/\/ the default, same as Nexus(storage: .archetype)","let churning = Nexus(storage: .sparseSet) \/\/ for heavy add\/remove churn"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Both storages offer the same API with the same observable behavior: generational entity identifiers, events, the structural lock and its traps, families, ","type":"text"},{"code":"forEach(reading:writing:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", spans, snapshots, cloning and the entity state machine. Every test of the package runs against both. What differs is where the components live in memory, and with it what is cheap.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","type":"reference"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference"},{"text":", so ","type":"text"},{"code":"Nexus()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" uses it. Choose ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" explicitly for workloads dominated by heavy component add and remove churn (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","type":"reference"},{"text":"). There is no storage protocol: the set of storages is closed, and a nexus switches on its storage once per call, so each storage compiles to concrete code.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"The sparse-set storage","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-sparse-set-storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" keeps one dense array per component type, a paged sparse index per type that maps an entity to its slot in that array, and a bitset of component types per entity. Adding or removing a component touches the data of that one type only, and no other component moves. Looking up one component is a sparse index read plus an array read.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating a family is the weak spot: the members of a family are stored in each component array in the order the components were added, so every extra component type costs a lookup per member, and the reads are scattered once the arrays were shuffled by churn.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"The archetype storage","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-archetype-storage"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype","type":"reference"},{"text":" follows the design of ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","type":"reference"},{"text":": entities with exactly the same component types live in one table, with a column (an array) per component type. An index maps every entity to its table and row. Tables are created when a component set appears first, and adding or removing one component type moves the entity’s row to another table along a cached edge of the table graph.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Iterating a family visits the tables that match it, and walks their columns linearly: no lookup per member and a sequential read per component. The list of matching tables is cached per family, which the nexus lists when the family is created and extends when a new table appears. A table that became empty stays alive, along with its columns and its entry in the cached lists, where an iteration skips it. Cleaning the nexus with ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/clear()"},{"text":" drops all tables.","type":"text"}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"In flecs this is the default, and sparse components are the opt-in trait (","type":"text"},{"code":"Sparse","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"): “Sparse components are stored outside of tables, which means they do not have to be moved”, trading query speed for component add and remove speed (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","type":"reference"},{"text":"). Fireblade 1.x was the reverse, a sparse set per component type; the two storages make that a choice per nexus instead of per component.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"anchor":"What-the-numbers-say","text":"What the numbers say","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Measured with 10 000 entities, release build, Apple silicon, wall clock p50 per pass (","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"make benchmark"},{"text":", see ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Benchmarks\/"},{"text":"):","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"alignments":["left","right","right"],"rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Case","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Sparse set","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Archetype","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"11 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2.5 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"18 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"4.3 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, B, C, D)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"31 μs","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"7.7 μs","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading: A, writing: B)"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"17 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4.4 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"forEach(reading: A, B, writing: C)","type":"codeVoice"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"23 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"6.1 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 10% of the entities match"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"3.6 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1.3 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 100 000 entities with shuffled storage order"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"227 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"27 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 reads, 1 024 different component sets"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"18 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"11 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Parameter pack, 5 reads and 2 writes"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 200 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 800 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Plain "},{"code":"for","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" over a family, 2 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"455 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Random "},{"code":"entity.get","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" of one component, 10 000 lookups"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"334 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"345 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a component to each entity and remove it again, 10 000 entities"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"2 180 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4 900 μs"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Create and destroy 1 000 entities with 7 components"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"1 730 μs"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"2 510 μs","type":"text"}]}]]],"header":"row","type":"table"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Fireblade 1.x needed 480 μs for the plain iteration of one component and 1 220 μs for two (","type":"text"},{"code":"IterOnlyOneComponent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"IterOnlyTwoComponents","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"). Both storages iterate without any allocation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Iterating with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"forEach(reading:writing:)"},{"text":" is 1.6 to 8 times faster on the archetype storage: about 4 times in the plain case, 8 times when the sparse-set arrays are shuffled against each other, and least when the entities are spread over many small tables.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Changing the component set of an entity costs about twice as much on the archetype storage: the whole row moves. An entity that changes its component set less than once in a few frames is far ahead on iteration; a world that toggles a component on most entities every frame is better off with the sparse set.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Plain ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for"},{"text":" iteration and random access cost the same on both: they look every component up per entity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Entity creation and destruction are a bit slower on the archetype storage, because the row of every component moves with the entity.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Which storage to pick","anchor":"Which-storage-to-pick"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The default is the archetype storage: it iterates faster (see ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","type":"reference"},{"text":"), and iteration is what most worlds spend their time on.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The trade-off: the archetype storage buys iteration speed with the cost of moving a row whenever the component set of an entity changes. Prefer ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/sparseSet","type":"reference"},{"text":" when the workload is dominated by heavy add and remove churn, for example toggling a component on most entities every frame. This matches flecs, where sparse components are the opt-in trait for components that are added and removed often.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Differences you can observe","anchor":"Differences-you-can-observe"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Iteration order.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" The sparse-set storage visits the members of a family in the order of the family’s member list, the archetype storage table by table and row by row, and rows move when entities change tables. Neither order is a contract; use "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" or your own key if you need one."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Single-type spans.","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(writing:_:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" view one contiguous array. On the archetype storage a type is stored in one column per table, so if entities with different component sets have the type, the span views a temporary copy made table by table (and the writing variant stores it back when the closure returns, also when it throws). That costs one allocation and a copy per call, and nothing can observe the difference while the closure runs, because the type is locked."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Family spans."}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Family\/forEachComponentSpan(reading:writing:_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" passes one batch per matching table on the archetype storage, however the nexus was used before; the sparse-set storage passes shorter batches after churn. Both visit every member exactly once, and the closure must be correct for any batch size."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the spans.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"kind":"article","metadata":{"role":"article","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"FirebladeECS"}],"title":"Choosing a storage"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Essentials","anchor":"Essentials","identifiers":["doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReadingAndWritingComponents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ComponentMacro","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/SavingAndLoadingScenes","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/MigratingToFirebladeECS2","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEvent","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind"]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS":{"type":"topic","title":"FirebladeECS","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs","abstract":[{"text":"A lightweight, fast and easy to use Entity-Component System in Swift.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#What-the-numbers-say","type":"topic","title":"What the numbers say","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#What-the-numbers-say","kind":"section"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind/default":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/default","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The storage "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)"},{"type":"text","text":" uses by default: "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind\/archetype"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"default","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind\/default","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"let"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"`default`"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Nexus"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS5NexusC11StorageKindO","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"StorageKind"}]},"https://github.com/SanderMertens/flecs/blob/master/docs/ComponentTraits.md":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md","type":"link","title":"component traits","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"component traits"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/SanderMertens\/flecs\/blob\/master\/docs\/ComponentTraits.md"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventDelegate":{"fragments":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"NexusEventDelegate"}],"type":"topic","title":"NexusEventDelegate","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventdelegate","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A delegate for receiving Nexus events and errors."}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEventDelegate","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"https://www.flecs.dev/flecs/md_docs_2Queries.html":{"url":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html","type":"link","title":"flecs","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"flecs"}],"identifier":"https:\/\/www.flecs.dev\/flecs\/md_docs_2Queries.html"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/componentSpan(reading:_:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/componentSpan(reading:_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Gives "},{"code":"body","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" read access to all components of a type as one contiguous "},{"code":"Span","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"componentSpan(reading:_:)","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/componentspan(reading:_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"componentSpan"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"reading"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":".Type, ("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:s4SpanV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Span"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"C"},{"kind":"text","text":">) "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"rethrows"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Result"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ReactingToNexusEvents":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ReactingToNexusEvents","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Observe structural changes and, on request, changes of component values."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Reacting to Nexus events","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/reactingtonexusevents"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Entity/identifier":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Entity\/identifier","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The unique entity identifier."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"identifier","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/entity\/identifier","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:12FirebladeECS16EntityIdentifierV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"EntityIdentifier"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/GettingStartedWithFirebladeECS","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn the API and key types Fireblade provides to compose your game or app logic."}],"type":"topic","kind":"article","title":"Getting started with Fireblade ECS","role":"article","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/gettingstartedwithfirebladeecs"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/NexusEventMask":{"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"NexusEventMask","kind":"identifier"}],"type":"topic","title":"NexusEventMask","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventMask","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexuseventmask","abstract":[{"text":"The kinds of events a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/NexusEventDelegate","type":"reference"},{"text":" subscribes to.","type":"text"}],"role":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"NexusEventMask","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick":{"url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/choosingastorage#Which-storage-to-pick","type":"topic","title":"Which storage to pick","abstract":[],"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/ChoosingAStorage#Which-storage-to-pick","kind":"section"},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/StorageKind":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/StorageKind","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The storage a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus"},{"type":"text","text":" keeps its entities and components in."}],"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"StorageKind"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"Nexus.StorageKind","role":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/firebladeecs\/nexus\/storagekind","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"enum"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"StorageKind"}]},"doc://FirebladeECS/documentation/FirebladeECS/Nexus/init(storage:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/FirebladeECS\/documentation\/FirebladeECS\/Nexus\/init(storage:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Initializes a new Nexus."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","title":"init(storage:)","role":"symbol","url"